errors.Unwrap(Title(d)) removes the *OpError link: at run time the result is
the bare doc.ErrNoTitle. errors.Unwrap is not an intrinsic; its body is analysed
and ends in a field load, which is unresolved(memory) by design (fields are never
tracked). Expected: Unresolved entries only, one per Unwrap Candidate of the
program (*fmt.wrapError, *xerr.OpError); never an empty set, never the wrapped form.
-- args --
transform/transform.go:@peel
